From faf6b15f01641c06239bc004b4cce38b03b613e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: facetimehd downstream <facetimehd-downstream@localhost>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 01/19] driver: drop pre-5.15 compatibility branches and dead
 code

The fork targets Linux 5.15 and newer, which is the floor its CI builds
against, so the version-gated branches below that are unreachable and only
make the surrounding code harder to read. Remove them and modernise the
idioms they were hiding:

  - vb2 queue_setup loses the 4.4/4.5/4.8 signature variants, and the
    vb2_alloc_ctx dance goes with them: q->dev is how the DMA device is
    passed since 4.8.
  - VFL_TYPE_GRABBER, pci-aspm.h, pci_set_consistent_dma_mask() and the
    device_caps guard are all gone.
  - pci_enable_msi()/pci_disable_msi() become pci_alloc_irq_vectors()/
    pci_free_irq_vectors(), and the interrupt is no longer requested with
    IRQF_SHARED - that was needed for the legacy INTx line the old helper
    could fall back to, and a single MSI vector is never shared.
  - mdelay() becomes msleep()/usleep_range() on every wait long enough to
    matter; none of them are called from atomic context.
  - __attribute__((packed)) becomes __packed, the ioctl/vb2/file operation
    tables become const, strcpy()/strncpy() into fixed V4L2 names become
    strscpy(), __FUNCTION__ becomes __func__, and pr_err() becomes
    dev_err() where a device is in hand.

Also delete what nothing uses: struct buf_ctx and struct fthd_plane, the
GET_IOMMU_PAGES macro, the setup_buffers() and fthd_buffer_queued_handler()
declarations, an unused response_size in terminal_handler(), and the
snprintf()-built hex-dump prefix in the camera-config loop.

No functional change beyond the MSI request flag.
